      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/e19adc/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-08-15T14:11:30.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Just got my Kickstarter, with the two packs of minifigs. They look great, but they're made of a material that is&nbsp;<span>unfamiliar to me</span><span>. (Admittedly, the last time I painted minis, I was painting with Testors enamels on RP lead figures or plastic Space Marines. Ye olde tabletop dino goes \"Roar\", I know, I know...)</span></p><p>I was just wondering if anyone from GTG or anyone else who has these can tell me what kinds of paints should be safe to use on these figures. (The thought of Legacy melting in my hands when I apply paint thinner after an inevitable screw-up is painful, to say the least.)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thanks!</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:11.090Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
